# Test layer rules

- Organize tests by layer: `DomainTests` validates domain behavior only; `ApplicationTests` validates application flows.
- Each test should assert one behavior; use readable naming such as `Given_When_Then` or an equivalent convention.
- Use mocks/stubs only for boundary dependencies; avoid unnecessary mocks in pure domain tests.
- Assertions should state intent clearly; control time and randomness to avoid flaky tests.
- Use builders/factories to reduce duplicated test data.
- On failure, leave minimal but meaningful fixtures or logs that point to the root cause.
- Test code must follow the same formatting and `#region` conventions as production code.
